From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:12:32 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 35/35] fix: a code window image may differ in one check word
 in 64

On a Switch, Master Mode's image went from 6 to 11 to 12 differing data
words in one session, close to the fixed 16. Measured over UN5's images, one
overlay's images differ in up to ~1200 check words on shared offsets (data
the recompiler took for code), different overlays in over 36,000, and those
already fail the leading words. The limit is now one check word in 64, at
least 16.

Battle replay and intro movie frames identical; shop after Free Battle and
Master Mode run on the Mac.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 runtime/src/dispatch.cpp | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/runtime/src/dispatch.cpp b/runtime/src/dispatch.cpp
index 19f0d57..5fd695d 100644
--- a/runtime/src/dispatch.cpp
+++ b/runtime/src/dispatch.cpp
@@ -77,17 +77,20 @@ const Instance *in_place(const Instance &i) {
 // The recompiler takes for code some words that are data: UN5's battle overlay
 // holds a table of heap pointers among its functions, which every battle
 // fills differently, and the shop, loaded over it, keeps them. A window image
-// whose leading words are in place may differ from memory in up to
-// kStaleWords such words; an image of other content differs in thousands.
-// The image differing least serves, and its differing words are not checked.
-constexpr std::uint32_t kStaleWords = 16;
+// whose leading words are in place may differ from memory in up to one check
+// word in kStaleShare. UN5's images of one overlay differ in up to ~1200 such
+// words (of 300,000-500,000), and Master Mode rewrites more as it is played;
+// images of different overlays differ in over 36,000. The image differing
+// least serves, and its differing words are not checked.
+constexpr std::uint32_t kStaleShare = 64;
 
 bool window_image(const ModuleInfo &m, Instance &out) {
     if (!leads_in_place(m, m.fixed_base)) return false;
+    const std::uint32_t limit = std::max(16u, m.check_count / kStaleShare);
     std::vector<std::uint32_t> stale;
     for (std::uint32_t k = 0; k < m.check_count; ++k) {
         if (ld32(m.fixed_base + m.checks[2 * k]) == m.checks[2 * k + 1]) continue;
-        if (stale.size() == kStaleWords) return false;
+        if (stale.size() == limit || (out.module && stale.size() >= out.stale.size())) return false;
         stale.push_back(k);
     }
     if (out.module && out.stale.size() <= stale.size()) return false;
